{"type":"text","timestamp":1791297187644,"sessionID":"ses_eee5f9046ffeVLwOEN4GFd84e2","part":{"id":"prt_111a1db39001Acq04NCaEWY8AR","messageID":"msg_111a1c92b001bdbKAh7xrxN7PH","sessionID":"ses_eee5f9046ffeVLwOEN4GFd84e2","type":"text","text":"Done. The file `records.json` contains **40** records.\n\nDetails of the extraction:\n\n- **Daemon log:** SHP-1001 to SHP-1018 (18 records). I removed the duplicate SHP-1005 retransmit line. I excluded SHP-1077 because the log marks it VOIDED before pickup.\n- **Shift notes:** SHP-1019 to SHP-1030 (12 records). I excluded SHP-1098 because it is only planned.\n- **Whiteboard table:** SHP-1031 to SHP-1036 (6 records).\n- **Legacy terminal:** SHP-1037 to SHP-1040 (4 records). I converted the DD/MM/YYYY dates to YYYY-MM-DD and parsed \"1,250.5 KG\" as the number 1250.5.\n\nI normalized carriers to lower case without service suffixes (for example, \"FedEx Ground\" → `fedex`, \"DHL Express\" → `dhl`). All weights are JSON numbers. All destinations are in Title Case. The validation script confirmed unique ids, correct field sets, and valid formats. The source file `dispatch_log.txt` is unchanged.","time":{"start":1791297182521,"end":1791297187639}}}
